# Prettier reformats the bodies of inline <script> blocks. index.html pins those
# by sha256 hash in its Content-Security-Policy, so formatting it invalidates
# both hashes and the browser then refuses to run them - silently. One of them is
# the theme bootstrap, so the visible symptom is the flash-of-wrong-theme it
# exists to prevent, with nothing in the console to explain it.
#
# scripts/check_csp_hashes.py catches this in CI; this file stops `npm run
# format` from causing it in the first place.
frontend/index.html

# 80 KB, one large inline script, no CSP of its own. Reformatting it is a large
# diff with no benefit.
frontend/worldcup.html

